WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.780 --> 00:00:06.980
You're officially invited to the wedding
of Brooke and Joseph Cavanaugh.

00:00:17.060 --> 00:00:19.560
Holy crap, this season of
"American Horror Story" is -

00:00:19.720 --> 00:00:21.540
don't say it, Think Story, don't jinx it -

00:00:21.800 --> 00:00:23.820
one of the best yet?

00:00:23.820 --> 00:00:29.000
Yes, I am absolutely loving the mystery
and 80's nostalgia AHS is pumping out.

00:00:29.180 --> 00:00:33.100
And this episode is filled with so
many tinfoil hat conspiracy theories,

00:00:33.220 --> 00:00:35.300
I feel like I'm in a Shyamalan movie.

00:00:35.500 --> 00:00:36.680
So we're gonna get right into it.

00:00:36.680 --> 00:00:39.960
And before we start, make sure to
like and subscribe with the bell on

00:00:40.020 --> 00:00:42.660
for the latest
"American Horror Story" updates.

00:00:42.760 --> 00:00:45.700
Episode 2 begins with
the arrival of Dr. Hopple.

00:00:45.840 --> 00:00:48.980
If you listen to the ominous
synthesizer music in the background,

00:00:48.980 --> 00:00:51.640
which I can't really play
or I'll get demonetized,

00:00:51.820 --> 00:00:55.620
you'll notice it's a throwback to John
Carpenter's score for "Halloween".

00:00:55.720 --> 00:00:59.420
She walks past the payphone Brooke
answered at the end of last episode.

00:00:59.520 --> 00:01:02.980
The same phone where someone
answered, saying they were Satan.

00:01:03.040 --> 00:01:07.880
Last episode also ended with the Night
Stalker coming out from the forest near Brooke,

00:01:07.880 --> 00:01:11.580
but we never saw Brooke acknowledge
him, so he's still biding his time.

00:01:11.600 --> 00:01:16.660
Hopple stops in front of the Camp Redwood map
and seems to point to this area near the bottom,

00:01:16.820 --> 00:01:18.760
likely where the main camp is situated,

00:01:18.840 --> 00:01:22.140
before she invites herself
into Margaret Booth's cabin.

00:01:22.200 --> 00:01:25.400
And for someone who is a Christian,
Margaret isn't too welcoming.

00:01:25.560 --> 00:01:28.200
This is oddly juxtaposed later in the episode

00:01:28.200 --> 00:01:34.280
when the Night Stalker literally breaks into the
cabin and she welcomes him with open arms. Weird.

00:01:34.380 --> 00:01:37.320
Hopple tries to convince
Margaret to shut down the camp

00:01:37.320 --> 00:01:41.380
due to the recent escape of
Benjamin Richter aka Mr Jingles,

00:01:41.500 --> 00:01:43.200
who is likely coming for her.

00:01:43.260 --> 00:01:47.840
After all, he apparently has an
obsessive revenge fantasy to kill Margaret,

00:01:48.020 --> 00:01:51.980
the lone survivor of the Camp
Redwood massacre 14 years ago.

00:01:52.020 --> 00:01:55.080
Margaret shows her she's
prepared, taking out a handgun,

00:01:55.300 --> 00:01:59.580
and you know whenever they show a gun,
it will almost inevitably be used later on.

00:01:59.660 --> 00:02:05.760
I also found it a bit suspicious for a camp leader, someone who is around children all day, to own a gun.

00:02:05.820 --> 00:02:08.740
And also considering she
thinks Jingles is locked away.

00:02:08.860 --> 00:02:10.940
Then again, this is
"American Horror Story".

00:02:11.040 --> 00:02:13.800
Margaret refuses to
budge and Hopple storms off

00:02:13.800 --> 00:02:20.240
only to have her tire torn to shreds by this
nasty-looking thing, planted here by Mr. Jingles.

00:02:20.240 --> 00:02:23.840
He's still riding in Roy's truck,
which he stole in episode 1

00:02:23.840 --> 00:02:25.560
and ends up killing her, saying,

00:02:27.420 --> 00:02:29.280
And slices off her ear.

00:02:29.360 --> 00:02:32.920
Now, this is the first time we've actually
seen him do this since the escape.

00:02:33.200 --> 00:02:36.500
We never saw it with the
orderly or Ed from the gas station.

00:02:36.700 --> 00:02:42.000
This either means it was simply never shown
or that he only takes ears from certain people.

00:02:42.120 --> 00:02:47.800
Remember that Hopple is - ahem - or was the
chief psychologist at Red Meadows Asylum

00:02:47.800 --> 00:02:49.200
where Jingles was kept.

00:02:49.280 --> 00:02:52.540
She likely was in charge of
administering any treatment to him.

00:02:52.780 --> 00:02:56.900
And if Hopple was, say, doing illegal
experiments or therapies on him,

00:02:57.060 --> 00:02:59.260
which we see in the
season preview video,

00:02:59.440 --> 00:03:02.040
she'd have an ulterior
motive to stop Jingles.

00:03:02.320 --> 00:03:07.500
Jingles may be the only one who knows the
truth about what is really happening at that asylum.

00:03:07.560 --> 00:03:11.640
This would mean Jingles killing Hopple
wasn't just a random cold-blooded murder,

00:03:11.880 --> 00:03:14.200
it was revenge for years of torture.

00:03:14.300 --> 00:03:18.180
While the other counselors party it
up, Brooke is fixated on the television,

00:03:18.300 --> 00:03:20.660
which reports the
murder at Roy's gas station.

00:03:20.660 --> 00:03:26.340
The sheriff himself isn't sure if this murder is any way associated with the string of murders happening in L.A.,

00:03:26.340 --> 00:03:27.980
the ones by the Night Stalker.

00:03:28.120 --> 00:03:30.160
Now, I didn't mention
this in my last video,

00:03:30.200 --> 00:03:33.580
but he is based off real-life
serial killer Ricky Ramirez,

00:03:33.580 --> 00:03:41.740
who terrorized L.A. and San Francisco with a string of home invasion murders from June 1984 to August 1985,

00:03:41.740 --> 00:03:43.660
in which he was convicted of 13.

00:03:43.660 --> 00:03:45.500
When Brooke expresses her concerns,

00:03:45.500 --> 00:03:49.440
the others seem more interested in the
"Where's the beef?" commercial than her plight.

00:03:49.440 --> 00:03:50.660
"Hey, where's the beef?"

00:03:50.660 --> 00:03:55.080
But before anything can happen, Margaret
interrupts, telling them it's all time for bed.

00:03:55.340 --> 00:03:57.580
And we get my favorite line of the episode:

00:03:59.780 --> 00:04:06.060
We get more religious talk from Margaret about how this place is used to cleanse the soul and wash away the sin.

00:04:06.060 --> 00:04:09.540
It's usually the religious zealots who
are willing to take things too extreme,

00:04:09.600 --> 00:04:13.960
so all this talk about "cleansing the
soul" raises major red flags to me.

00:04:14.060 --> 00:04:17.180
Speaking of which, a literal
red flag right outside her cabin.

00:04:17.260 --> 00:04:21.500
Montana tries to console Brooke by
comparing her almost getting killed to fat camp.

00:04:21.680 --> 00:04:22.940
"It's a fat camp!"

00:04:23.160 --> 00:04:27.000
And even though Montana isn't the best at
this, we know her heart is in the right place.

00:04:31.420 --> 00:04:35.980
This line here is very interesting and makes
us even doubt if Brooke is telling the truth.

00:04:36.260 --> 00:04:39.280
Up until this point, no one
else has seen the Night Stalker.

00:04:39.280 --> 00:04:43.600
But he is real, since we later see him chat
with Margaret and fight with Mr. Jingles.

00:04:43.860 --> 00:04:49.780
And yes, I'm still holding onto the theory that there
is more to Mr. Jingles than meets the eye - or ear.

00:04:49.860 --> 00:04:53.740
We then get my favorite scene of
the episode: American Red Wedding.

00:04:53.740 --> 00:04:55.340
Yes, Brooke was set to be married,

00:04:55.340 --> 00:05:01.360
when her jealous husband-to-be brutally murders the best man and her dad, thinking Brooke cheated on him.

00:05:01.540 --> 00:05:05.180
But Brooke, having a terrible fear of the
dark, just wanted someone to be there,

00:05:05.180 --> 00:05:08.080
since she didn't want to see her
husband the same day of the wedding.

00:05:08.080 --> 00:05:11.020
This is why I have gamophobia:
fear of marriage.

00:05:11.020 --> 00:05:12.180
Kidding, I'm single.

00:05:12.400 --> 00:05:14.052
DM me, I'm so terribly alone.

00:05:14.140 --> 00:05:17.280
Back in 1984, Brooke
reiterates that she never cheated,

00:05:17.280 --> 00:05:22.880
and maybe it was her sense of vulnerability or
the fact Montana had a bunch of Pabst Blue Ribbons,

00:05:23.040 --> 00:05:26.440
she goes in for the kiss, which
Brooke doesn't take too well.

00:05:26.540 --> 00:05:28.080
It's shower time!

00:05:28.400 --> 00:05:29.560
"Let's go take hot shower!"

00:05:29.560 --> 00:05:35.200
And we get these creepy voyeur shots of the boys,
which is totally reminiscent of 70's and 80's horror.

00:05:35.580 --> 00:05:39.160
Trevor tells the guys what he was
up to with Montana last episode

00:05:39.240 --> 00:05:41.660
when Xavier runs
off to grab a towel.

00:05:41.820 --> 00:05:45.740
Margaret turns off the power in what
I'm assuming is mandatory bedtime,

00:05:45.740 --> 00:05:47.600
judging by how
she checks her watch.

00:05:47.600 --> 00:05:51.500
She's the only one who has the key
here, which might come into play later on.

00:05:51.680 --> 00:05:57.240
Xavier is grabbed by a porn producer in the
forest at night, a line you really never want to hear.

00:05:57.340 --> 00:06:00.260
His name is Blake, who
we'll come to know as daddy.

00:06:00.600 --> 00:06:01.960
"What the hell, daddy?"

00:06:01.960 --> 00:06:04.020
It looks like I have some competition.

00:06:04.140 --> 00:06:05.460
Daddy loves you very much.

00:06:05.460 --> 00:06:09.420
Blake is obsessed with Xavier,
comparing him to a Rembrandt painting.

00:06:09.620 --> 00:06:16.440
For his help in getting him clean, Blake coerced Xavier
to do a gay porno, which he now uses as blackmail,

00:06:16.660 --> 00:06:20.900
blackmail which could completely destroy
his chances of becoming a famous star.

00:06:20.980 --> 00:06:22.680
But Xavier sees a way out.

00:06:22.820 --> 00:06:27.100
If he can offer Blake something better,
a man even bigger than John Holmes,

00:06:27.100 --> 00:06:31.880
a porn star known for his, ahem,
endowment, he could be scot-free.

00:06:32.000 --> 00:06:35.220
And there just so happens to be
a guy like that at Camp Redwood.

00:06:35.360 --> 00:06:38.740
In the shower Chet can't seem
to take his eyes off the prize.

00:06:38.900 --> 00:06:41.660
This might also be the fact
that he's been taking steroids,

00:06:41.660 --> 00:06:44.540
and we know what kind of
effect that can have down there.

00:06:44.840 --> 00:06:45.560
"It shrinks?"

00:06:46.820 --> 00:06:50.980
Our favorite porn producer Blake also
can't seem to take his eyes off Trevor,

00:06:51.140 --> 00:06:53.120
getting him killed in the process.

00:06:53.260 --> 00:06:57.580
Notice how we see Mr. Jingles'
leather gloves here, but nothing else.

00:06:57.720 --> 00:07:03.000
It's entirely possible that this isn't Mr.
Jingles at all, rather one of his copycats.

00:07:03.020 --> 00:07:08.500
In my season to come preview video, I noted how
we'll eventually come to see multiple Mr. Jingles',

00:07:08.500 --> 00:07:12.000
and that Margaret herself could
be posing as Jingles as well.

00:07:12.080 --> 00:07:17.360
Remember she did just turn off the lights, carries
a bunch of keys on her, and hates those who sin.

00:07:17.480 --> 00:07:19.280
And Blake is a prime candidate.

00:07:19.280 --> 00:07:22.500
At the docks, Brooke gets some
fresh air after her kiss with Montana,

00:07:22.620 --> 00:07:24.940
and comes across
Hopple's floating corpse.

00:07:25.140 --> 00:07:30.920
But look at this, if we compare the shot from episode 2 to the one we saw in the season preview video,

00:07:31.020 --> 00:07:32.420
they are very different.

00:07:32.420 --> 00:07:35.280
Now, this is either just a
mistake on the part of AHS,

00:07:35.280 --> 00:07:40.560
or it's hinting that what Brooke is seeing may
not be real, or at least not the way she sees it.

00:07:40.720 --> 00:07:44.080
It's possible we could see this same
event replayed in the later episode,

00:07:44.080 --> 00:07:47.000
but from a different
perspective or with new information.

00:07:47.060 --> 00:07:51.280
I have a theory I'm gonna talk about a
little bit later that could also fit into this.

00:07:51.280 --> 00:07:55.960
She's interrupted by the Night Stalker, but is
able to escape. But let's hold on for a second.

00:07:56.100 --> 00:07:58.600
Brooke isn't stabbed
by the Night Stalker here,

00:07:58.640 --> 00:08:01.860
but in the season to come video
when she's being chased by him,

00:08:01.980 --> 00:08:04.540
you can clearly see a
stab wound on her shoulder.

00:08:04.660 --> 00:08:09.060
Now there could be an explanation for this.
It's possible this could happen in a later episode.

00:08:09.140 --> 00:08:14.480
But it's when the Night Stalker bumps into the
hiker that we really need to get our tinfoil hats on.

00:08:14.620 --> 00:08:19.260
Also, can we just take a moment to acknowledge
that the hiker has a habit of bumping into things?

00:08:23.520 --> 00:08:26.340
Moving along, the hiker
says two important things:

00:08:26.560 --> 00:08:31.140
"You're not supposed to be here" and,
most telling, "Wait, I don't die here".

00:08:31.200 --> 00:08:33.320
And this is interesting,
because in the preview video,

00:08:33.360 --> 00:08:37.000
we see him getting knocked
out, possibly killed by Mr. Jingles.

00:08:37.180 --> 00:08:38.360
What does this mean?

00:08:38.520 --> 00:08:43.540
Well, there's a theory out there that everyone
at the camp in 1984 is a method actor,

00:08:43.540 --> 00:08:48.080
preparing for their roles in an upcoming
film about the original massacre.

00:08:48.160 --> 00:08:53.000
They are all staying in character and following
a series of events to better get into their roles.

00:08:53.160 --> 00:09:00.040
In episode 1, Xavier even says he's trained under Stella Adler, who was known for pioneering method acting,

00:09:00.200 --> 00:09:03.480
an acting technique in which the
actor does not break character.

00:09:03.640 --> 00:09:06.000
In the earlier preview clips that FX released,

00:09:06.060 --> 00:09:10.820
we also see the characters doing a screen
test and hitting marks on the cabin floor.

00:09:11.000 --> 00:09:15.860
This would mean that those grainy shots we've
seen that I previously said indicate a flashback

00:09:16.020 --> 00:09:20.160
might not be flashbacks at all, rather
actual film footage from the shoot.

00:09:20.260 --> 00:09:23.260
But it seems as though the Night
Stalker, according to the hiker,

00:09:23.260 --> 00:09:27.920
is not a part of this acting exercise,
as he literally guts the hiker.

00:09:28.180 --> 00:09:29.820
We'll get back to the hiker in a bit.

00:09:29.820 --> 00:09:33.980
Rita's in a nursing station, putting away stuff
in the middle of the night when the power is out,

00:09:33.980 --> 00:09:38.400
because I guess that's what you do,
when she's confronted by Mr. Jingles.

00:09:38.540 --> 00:09:42.680
This confrontation, however, we never
see, which I think is very important.

00:09:42.680 --> 00:09:47.180
Now if things couldn't get any weirder, we
have Brooke trying to call the police to no avail,

00:09:47.300 --> 00:09:52.360
when an apparent clone of the hiker appears,
only to be killed again by the Night Stalker.

00:09:52.520 --> 00:09:54.240
This guy isn't having a good time.

00:09:54.240 --> 00:09:58.840
But the Stalker takes the counselor's
badge to see he's from the 1970's.

00:09:58.900 --> 00:10:04.540
And check out his name, which is an anagram
for Jason Voorhees, the killer in "Friday the 13th".

00:10:04.540 --> 00:10:09.220
The Stalker seems to be freaked out by his
apparent return and heads off into the forest.

00:10:09.340 --> 00:10:12.840
Ray yells as everyone congregates
around the dead body of Blake.

00:10:13.000 --> 00:10:16.700
And you know, they have to check he's
actually dead by poking him with a stick.

00:10:16.740 --> 00:10:20.380
They hear the clanging of Mr. Jingles'
keys and run off towards the van,

00:10:20.560 --> 00:10:24.840
which directly transitions us to
another pair of keys held by Margaret.

00:10:24.960 --> 00:10:28.500
But more interesting here
is her holding a bottle of wine.

00:10:28.840 --> 00:10:33.760
Was she with someone, is she celebrating
something, or does she just need a nightcap?

00:10:33.960 --> 00:10:38.820
It's a conscious decision to show her with
this bottle, so expect it to come back later.

00:10:38.920 --> 00:10:42.800
Waiting for her is the Night Stalker, who
wants to know more about the hiker.

00:10:42.920 --> 00:10:45.260
You and me both, Ricky. You and me both.

00:10:45.420 --> 00:10:49.920
And for a guy who says he's the son of
Satan, Margaret is surprisingly helpful,

00:10:50.160 --> 00:10:51.400
curious about him.

00:10:53.820 --> 00:10:57.460
For Margaret, Ricky is a lost
soul, someone who can be saved.

00:10:57.560 --> 00:10:58.460
She tells him that

00:11:05.420 --> 00:11:08.500
So we're supposed to believe
Jesus brought back the hiker.

00:11:08.640 --> 00:11:11.340
But something tells me
there's a better answer out there.

00:11:11.420 --> 00:11:14.660
Margaret asked Ricky what the worst
thing that ever happened to him was,

00:11:14.900 --> 00:11:19.660
making this the fourth time in this episode alone
where characters have divulged their biggest trauma.

00:11:19.760 --> 00:11:22.800
First being Montana getting
felt up outside of Sam Goody's,

00:11:23.060 --> 00:11:24.620
second Brooke on her wedding,

00:11:24.820 --> 00:11:27.700
third Xavier and his drug/porn past,

00:11:27.780 --> 00:11:29.580
and finally Ricky's childhood.

00:11:29.640 --> 00:11:34.580
As a kid, Ricky's mother inhaled poisonous
fumes while she was pregnant at the boot factory.

00:11:34.660 --> 00:11:39.480
He had abusive parents, was knocked in the back of
the head by a swing, causing him to have seizures,

00:11:39.600 --> 00:11:44.820
and was exposed to gruesome real-life photos
of people his cousin Mike killed in Vietnam.

00:11:44.880 --> 00:11:46.680
Although this could be completely unrelated,

00:11:46.680 --> 00:11:50.900
both Jingles and Miriam Mead's father
in "Apocalypse" killed many in Vietnam.

00:11:51.020 --> 00:11:55.580
At 13, Ricky was present when Mike
shot his wife in a domestic dispute

00:11:55.640 --> 00:11:59.480
All of this is based off Ricky
Ramirez's real-life upbringing.

00:11:59.480 --> 00:12:03.020
For Ricky, pain is all he
has known - that and feet.

00:12:04.420 --> 00:12:07.540
Margaret tells him he doesn't have
to feel bad about what he's done.

00:12:20.020 --> 00:12:24.420
This sounds a lot like Margaret trying
to justify something she did in the past,

00:12:24.480 --> 00:12:29.340
but she goes on to say that in order to achieve
freedom from this pain, you need two things:

00:12:29.580 --> 00:12:30.980
God and trauma.

00:12:31.180 --> 00:12:36.300
So she agrees to look into the hiker if he
hunts down Mr. Jingles and leaves the rest alone.

00:12:36.500 --> 00:12:39.300
She's basically using him to get to Jingles.

00:12:39.400 --> 00:12:43.460
The counselors decide to get the hell
out of dodge by getting into Xavier's van.

00:12:43.780 --> 00:12:47.700
And why are they letting Xavier drive
again? Did they learn nothing last episode?

00:12:47.700 --> 00:12:49.620
Notice here this cigarette brand Brezza,

00:12:49.620 --> 00:12:53.780
which is a common prop name for
a cigarette brand used in film and television

00:12:54.000 --> 00:12:57.940
and can be seen in shows like
"Lost" and FX's own "You're the Worst".

00:12:57.940 --> 00:13:00.040
This is either AHS using it as a prop,

00:13:00.100 --> 00:13:04.420
or if we go with the "This is a movie"
narrative, it could be a prop on a set.

00:13:04.420 --> 00:13:07.840
The van ends up crashing into
Margaret's after narrowly missing Rita,

00:13:07.840 --> 00:13:10.740
who apparently escaped
that attack from Mr. Jingles.

00:13:10.920 --> 00:13:11.740
Interesting.

00:13:11.800 --> 00:13:13.500
Also, where is Chef Bertie?

00:13:13.620 --> 00:13:17.120
With the only chance of escape
Rita's car and Trevor's motorcycle,

00:13:17.120 --> 00:13:20.960
a motorcycle we see in the
previews taking off as Jingles watches,

00:13:21.140 --> 00:13:22.760
the group decides to split up,

00:13:22.960 --> 00:13:25.740
because it wouldn't be a
horror show unless they split up.

00:13:25.860 --> 00:13:30.760
Margaret ends up finding the hiker in the
woods, and there is a lot of fun stuff to unpack here.

00:13:31.000 --> 00:13:35.620
First, he says that Margaret looks "so
different", which could mean two things:

00:13:35.620 --> 00:13:38.120
A, she's just changed a lot in 14 years,

00:13:38.280 --> 00:13:43.760
or B, if you believe these are all actors, that the
Margaret here is an actress playing the real Margaret.

00:13:43.760 --> 00:13:49.640
One of the first things Margaret asks, which I find rather suspicious, is what he saw the night of the massacre.

00:13:49.820 --> 00:13:51.954
If Margaret was the actual killer,

00:13:52.120 --> 00:13:57.320
the hiker could possibly be the only one
who knows the truth aside from Mr. Jingles.

00:13:57.380 --> 00:14:02.220
It appears that the hiker did see Margaret
the night of the murder, but only the aftermath.

00:14:02.220 --> 00:14:04.500
He never saw her committing the actual act.

00:14:04.800 --> 00:14:08.080
He ran away, only to be
killed, supposedly, by Jingles.

00:14:08.300 --> 00:14:10.380
Now, two things could
have happened here:

00:14:10.600 --> 00:14:13.180
Margaret told Jingles
that the hiker was the killer,

00:14:13.260 --> 00:14:16.760
and Jingles went after him only
for Margaret to frame him later,

00:14:16.880 --> 00:14:20.520
or that Margaret herself dressed
up as Jingles and killed the hiker.

00:14:20.800 --> 00:14:24.620
After all, the hiker said he only
heard the keys of Mr. Jingles.

00:14:24.620 --> 00:14:30.360
This whole thing of the hiker being unjustly killed could explain why his ghost has remained at Camp Redwood.

00:14:30.360 --> 00:14:34.480
AHS is no stranger to having ghost
characters with unfinished business.

00:14:34.580 --> 00:14:37.540
This can be seen heavily in
season one's "Murder House".

00:14:37.600 --> 00:14:40.300
Brooke Ray, Chet and
Rita check out the infirmary

00:14:40.300 --> 00:14:43.780
while Trevor, Xavier and
Montana head back to the cabins.

00:14:43.920 --> 00:14:47.171
Xavier totally breaks down
saying everything is his fault,

00:14:47.220 --> 00:14:51.780
when the episode ends while two
figures bang simultaneously on both doors.

00:14:52.000 --> 00:14:55.700
We do see the Night Stalker head
toward the infirmary and a few shots prior,

00:14:55.700 --> 00:14:59.880
we see Jingles outside near the
cabins where Montana and Xavier are.

00:14:59.960 --> 00:15:04.560
We also know Margaret is somewhere in the woods
with the hiker, and Chef Bertie is nowhere to be found.

00:15:04.640 --> 00:15:07.351
You basically have a 1 in 4
chance of guessing who it could be,

00:15:07.600 --> 00:15:11.880
unless, of course, we have a 5th unknown
new character banging on the door.

00:15:12.080 --> 00:15:16.740
Remember the newscasts reported the murder
at Roy's gas station just a few hours ago,

00:15:16.740 --> 00:15:21.220
so it's possible we could get a sheriff or
detective working their way to Camp Redwood,

00:15:21.300 --> 00:15:26.400
seeing as the counselors were one of the last
people to see Patrick Swayze's brother alive.

00:15:26.400 --> 00:15:31.260
This episode was chock-full of new
developments, but left us with even more mystery.

00:15:31.420 --> 00:15:36.040
I want to hear your theories below, or you can
reach out to me on Twitter @ThinkStoryYT.

00:15:36.120 --> 00:15:40.000
Make sure to like and subscribe
and check out my other AHS videos.

00:15:40.000 --> 00:15:43.380
I'm here all season and I'll
see you next week for episode 3.

00:15:43.680 --> 00:15:45.200
Until next time remember,

00:15:45.540 --> 00:15:47.000
"What the hell, daddy"

00:15:47.000 --> 00:15:48.640
No! Daddy loves you very much.

